ogical activities, including its presence in extracts studied for cellular health. The strongest evidence so far comes from human observational studies (Oxford level 2b) looking at the complex plant extracts that contain it.","structure_function":[{"claim_id":"antimicrobial","statement":"Early work points toward delta-guaiene playing a role in the antimicrobial properties of the plant extracts it inhabits.","evidence_level":"human_observational","basis":"This is based on two papers, including human observational and in vitro research.","eco":{"id":"ECO:0000180","label":"clinical study evidence"},"oxford":{"level":"2b","label":"individual cohort or observational study"},"evidence_lines":[{"design":"human_observational","eco":"ECO:0000180","papers":1},{"design":"in_vitro","eco":"ECO:0000181","papers":1}],"paper_count":2},{"claim_id":"cancer","statement":"Delta-guaiene is being studied for its potential role in supporting cellular health.","evidence_level":"human_observational","basis":"This rests on two human observational studies examining extracts containing this molecule.","eco":{"id":"ECO:0000180","label":"clinical study evidence"},"oxford":{"level":"2b","label":"individual cohort or observational study"},"evidence_lines":[{"design":"human_observational","eco":"ECO:0000180","papers":2}],"paper_count":2}],"hypothesized_benefits":[{"claim_id":"antimicrobial","area":"Antimicrobial activity","hypothesis":"Researchers are exploring whether delta-guaiene actively contributes to the antibacterial effects seen in patchouli and agarwood oils.","evidence_level":"human_observational","paper_count":2,"study_to_test_it":"A randomized, double-blind controlled trial applying a standardized delta-guaiene topical preparation to superficial skin abrasions to measure bacterial colonization rates over 7 days.","eco":{"id":"ECO:0000180","label":"clinical study evidence"},"oxford":{"level":"2b","label":"individual cohort or observational study"},"evidence_lines":[{"design":"human_observational","eco":"ECO:0000180","papers":1},{"design":"in_vitro","eco":"ECO:0000181","papers":1}]},{"claim_id":"cancer","area":"Cellular health","hypothesis":"Early observational work points toward a need to understand if delta-guaiene exerts direct protective effects on human cells.","evidence_level":"human_observational","paper_count":2,"study_to_test_it":"A randomized, placebo-controlled clinical trial measuring specific biomarkers of cellular oxidative stress and proliferation in a healthy cohort taking a standardized delta-guaiene supplement for 12 weeks.","eco":{"id":"ECO:0000180","label":"clinical study evidence"},"oxford":{"level":"2b","label":"individual cohort or observational study"},"evidence_lines":[{"design":"human_observational","eco":"ECO:0000180","papers":2}]}],"associated_conditions":[],"cautions":null,"evidence_at_a_glance":"Best evidence so far is human observational work (Oxford 2b) on plant extracts containing the molecule, with the rest being early lab and botanical research."}}
